# **The first movie that picks up a bonus object**, and with it `$80:FA79` --
# one of the five jump-table entries that were transcribed a round ago with no
# input in the project able to reach them.
#
# XDSJ is level 53, the same password `movies/level53.zmv` types; this replaces
# that movie's three gameplay lines with a route cut by `tools/fit_route.py` to
# the type-$38 objects at (450,567), (439,548) and (457,543). Their collision id
# is $2F ($80:CA30), and id $2F's entry in the player's jump table is $80:FA79 --
# kind 2, and $0500 of score.
#
# **It takes two of the three**, which the display list says plainly: at frame
# 3180 all three records are live, at 3190 the one at (439,548) is gone and a
# record with no collision id is drifting up-right from where it was, and at
# 3200 (450,567) has gone the same way. That drifting record is $82:E0B4, the
# thing `$80:FA79` spawns: the object's own sprite flying off in one of four
# diagonals for 21 ticks.
#
# Two awards of $0500 is also the first BCD score addition in the project that
# needs a decimal adjust, so `score_digit_carry` -- untaken by every input since
# `score_add` was ported -- is taken here.
#
# `zamn_cosim verify -f 3300` checks 49,098 calls with nothing declined and no
# divergence, and the coverage report gains `player_spawn_2`, `player_sfx_only`
# and `score_digit_carry`.
#
# Route: east and north out of the start, then the long climb up the x=475 lane
# and back down onto the objects. Eleven legs, all of them fitted.

